d flagged inferences for owner confirmation", "recommendation": "Scope: none. Settled mid-build (plan, \"Decisions made mid-build\"): (1) `built_chunks` was found to arm `critic_mode.short_plan_deferral` through `read_built`. The documented claim was changed to \"a gate may read it only to arm\", settled by \"do it right\". (2) At dispatch the subject walk always gets the interval's base, so R-11's note fires only when `git log` fails, and the unresolvable-`base:` cause is tested in plan_status alone. (3) `head_tree` is guarded by `gitstate.is_object_id`, and a malformed value reads every fragment as unreadable. The plan flags these inferences for this boundary review; the owner should confirm or correct them: what counts as a stub (content at the judged tree, not the commit that added it; a title alone is still a stub); which tree each reader uses; unreadable fragments count as unwritten and unparseable ones as written; and R-4 as decided, with scoped-only subjects for the certifying proposal and the fallback kept for the render tag. That last one changes what consumers see and is what the next-step finding above depends on. Every new capability traces to #1075's acceptance criteria or to R-4/R-11, and each is consumed: `is_fragment_path` and `is_unwritten_stub` by `_work_paths`; `ChunkProposal.notes` by `begin_review`'s `notes`, which the CLI prints; `_BranchWalk.head`, `scoped_named` and `all_named` by `built_report` and `chunk_proposal`; `propose_chunks` stays as a wrapper for critic_mode's Stop-path callers. No scope-trace gap.", "files": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-stub-not-built.md"], "fid": "R-9"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Learnings Cross-Check: three rules fired; no rules were added this cycle", "recommendation": "Scope: none. Files read, from `learnings-files --for-diff`: core.md, authoring.md, gates.md, hook-surface.md, release.md, tests.md. Rules that fired: core \"A coverage, completeness or absence claim 